# Gate contract

- After non-trivial Rust edits, run narrow checks first, then `/verify` (or the
  ordered gates in [verify-gates](../../skills/verify-gates/SKILL.md)) before
  claiming the change is merge-ready.
- Prefer [`.agents/hooks/run-verify.sh`](../../hooks/run-verify.sh) or the skill
  command list over pasted ad-hoc gate recipes.
- Never relax or bypass solely to hide failures:
  - [`clippy.toml`](../../../clippy.toml) thresholds
  - llvm-cov `--fail-under-lines 100`
  - dry-rs `--fail-on-findings` ([`scripts/dry-gate.sh`](../../../scripts/dry-gate.sh))
  - CRAP `--threshold strict` (8) ([`scripts/crap-gate.sh`](../../../scripts/crap-gate.sh))
  - tool pins in [`scripts/dry-score.rev`](../../../scripts/dry-score.rev) /
    [`scripts/crap-score.rev`](../../../scripts/crap-score.rev)
- Do not claim `/verify` or CI passed unless those commands were actually run
  and succeeded.
